{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T14:58:06.980Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T14:58:06.980Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-26T14:58:06.980Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause, from a tsx trace of the structured pass: (1) compact JSON: the quoted key 'password' inside the title string is judged by findStructuredSpellingMatches, whose value judge reads the concatenating PASSWORD_VALUE grammar without the enclosing-string close that GH-1775 added to flatMatches, so '${BUILD_PASSWORD}' runs on through the JSON string's closing quote into \",\"updated\":\"2026-11-25T00 (pretty JSON hides it because a quoted piece cannot cross the newline). (2) seven backslashes: the single-quoted raw (TOML/YAML) reading reused the escape-aware scanQuoted span, in which the seventh backslash escapes the final quote, so the literal read as unterminated and the quote counted as an eighth data character. Fix: the structured judge ends a text-read value at the enclosing string's close exactly as flatMatches does (cut, and recorded as the word end), through a lexer cursor with checkpoints every 1024 code units for keys nested in already-walked containers; the raw single-quoted reading ends at its own first quote. Differential over an 18,816-input corpus (8 keys x 26 values x quote styles x 7 serializations) against the published 2026.11.14 and 2026.11.25 bundles: 280 verdicts change, every one a finding to none, none on a literal-bearing value; 240 return to the 2026.11.14 verdict and the other 40 are bare $NAME and %NAME% references in quoted-key text, now placeholders as GH-1775 states for every serialization. '${BUILD_PASSWORD}(note)' was clean on both published versions (the parenthesis ends the word); attached literals such as '${BUILD_PASSWORD}<literal>' stay reported."}]}],"before_hash":"b02c21e7a016bb12411aee92dbce4a50d5c12fc77a0825d08a8c7cdda07b5dca","after_hash":"88728428bf29a39293ab2d235535cd2cf20ab1a50d17668cad095226a9f9b33e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2357535303981baf8f829bb06b48dd4b9e3efb3408f1c8f900fb414a183a1fec"}
